    ]
    decision """
        AKR authoring surfaces must expose typed per-kind slots, legal relations, canonical reference forms, and an executable recovery step before or with a rejected write. The MCP schema derives each kind's exact required and optional slots from the vocabulary, exposes scope as compact strings or a closed oneOf of typed forms, and rejects topic on non-normative kinds before ledger validation. Line-only source citations normalize trailing blank end lines to the same byte and line convention AKR-S022 validates. Scope globs matching no tracked path remain non-fatal authoring warnings. Successful MCP writes name the required build step. MCP reliability is verified through a long-lived installed subprocess running mixed successful and rejected calls, while setup verifies the installed binary and tells clients to reconnect after replacement.
